{"name":"Sea Loch","hex":"#6e99d1","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sea loch","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An arm of the sea, similar to a Norwegian fjord and to a firth. Most sea lochs are on the west coast of Scotland, Loch Torridon is one example."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sea_loch"}],"entries":[{"title":"Loch","blocks":[{"text":"Loch is a word meaning \"lake\" or \"sea inlet\" in Scottish and Irish Gaelic, subsequently borrowed into English. In Irish contexts, it often appears in the anglicized form \"lough\". A small loch is sometimes called a lochan. Lochs which connect to the sea may be called \"sea lochs\" or \"sea loughs\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Ben_Lomond_Scotland.jpg/330px-Ben_Lomond_Scotland.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loch","wikidata":"Q1172903"},{"title":"Sea","blocks":[{"text":"A sea is a very large body of salty water. The term has two distinct meanings. The first is the interconnected body of seawater that spans most of Earth, known as the sea or the ocean. The second is a named body of water: usually either a marginal sea, or a large, nearly landlocked body of water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/330px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea","wikidata":"Q165"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/LochLong%28StevePartridge%29Nov2007.jpg/330px-LochLong%28StevePartridge%29Nov2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/LochLong%28StevePartridge%29Nov2007.jpg/330px-LochLong%28StevePartridge%29Nov2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.or